Say where a Vulkan surface stops, in a release build.

With Skia on Vulkan in a GPU process of its own, chrome://gpu said Vulkan
was enabled and the page stayed black: no frame, no crash, no line in the
log. Every way VulkanSurface::Initialize can fail is a DLOG, which an
official build drops, and swapchain creation and presenting say nothing
at all.

On OHOS the Initialize failures are logged, and so are the surface's
format, the swapchain's creation or failure with its size, and the result
of the first present -- enough to tell a surface that never initialised
from a swapchain that never came up from frames that never got through.
At ERROR, because in the GPU process that is the level that reaches the
log.

Diagnostic; it comes out once Vulkan is understood here.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51.

diff --git a/gpu/vulkan/vulkan_surface.cc b/gpu/vulkan/vulkan_surface.cc
--- a/gpu/vulkan/vulkan_surface.cc
